def pancake_sort(nums):
    # Implement pancake sorting algorithm here
    def flip(arr, i):
        for k in range(i//2 + 1):
            arr[k], arr[i-k-1] = arr[i-k-1], arr[k]

    n = len(nums)
    while n > 1:
        max_index = nums.index(max(nums[:n]))
        if max_index != n - 1:
            flip(nums, max_index)
            flip(nums, n-1)
        n -= 1

# Example usage
if __name__ == "__main__":
    arr = [34, 56, 23, 12, 78]
    pancake_sort(arr)
    print("Sorted array is:", arr)
```

This solution follows the pancake sorting algorithm. It iteratively finds the maximum element in the unsorted portion of the list and moves it to the front by flipping the list up to that element's position. Then, it flips the entire sorted portion of the list to move the maximum element to its correct place. The process continues until the entire list is sorted.

